--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-Party Credits & Attribution
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

- TRS-OS:
  Ported and adapted for the Zilog eZ80 processor by Daniel Paul Martin.
  Upstream Website: https://danielpaulmartin.com

- TRSDOS 6.3.1 / LS-DOS 6.3:
  Originally developed by Logical Systems, Inc. and Misosys (Roy Soltoff, Dick Miller).
  Released into the public domain by Roy Soltoff via Tim Mann's Misosys archive.
  Website: https://www.tim-mann.org/misosys.html

- Agon Light Hardware Platform:
  Open-source 8-bit retrocomputer designed by Bernardo Kastrup (The Byte Attic)
  and manufactured by Olimex Ltd.
  Websites: https://www.thebyteattic.com/p/agon.html, https://github.com/OLIMEX/AgonLight2

- Agon Platform Quark MOS & VDP:
  Operating system and video display processor firmware developed by Dean Belfield
  and the Agon Platform community.
  Documentation: https://agonplatform.github.io/agon-docs/
  Repositories: https://github.com/AgonPlatform

- ez80asm:
  The canonical eZ80 assembler for the Agon platform developed by Jeroen Venema
  and the Agon Platform community.
  Repository: https://github.com/AgonPlatform/agon-ez80asm

- fab-agon-emulator:
  Agon Light software emulator developed by Tom Nairn.
  Repository: https://github.com/tomm/fab-agon-emulator
